Fix: replace variable sent to Twig EscaperRuntime escape method

TwigExtension::escapeFilter() computes $return as the properly
stringified/escaped-safe representation of $arg (handling scalars,
MarkupInterface, RenderableInterface, __toString()/toString() objects),
but then passes the raw, unconverted $arg to
EscaperRuntime::escape() for non-'html' strategies instead of $return.

This causes fatal TypeErrors (e.g. "Argument #4 ($autoescape) must be
of type bool, null given") and incorrect escaping of stringable
objects (e.g. Drupal\Core\Url) depending on what Twig's compiled
template code passes through.

Upstream: https://www.drupal.org/project/drupal/issues/3489668
Merge request !10329 (not yet committed as of this writing; status
"Needs work" pending additional test coverage, but the fix itself -
using the already-computed $return instead of $arg - is correct and
matches the file's own established pattern one line above).

Original patch by Julien JOYE, closes #3489668. Rebased here with a
depth-1 path (package root is web/core/, not the Drupal monorepo root
the original patch was generated from).

--- a/lib/Drupal/Core/Template/TwigExtension.php
+++ b/lib/Drupal/Core/Template/TwigExtension.php
@@ -487,7 +487,7 @@ public function escapeFilter(Environment $env, $arg, $strategy = 'html', $char
       if ($strategy == 'html') {
         return Html::escape($return);
       }
-      return $env->getRuntime(EscaperRuntime::class)->escape($arg, $strategy, $charset, $autoescape);
+      return $env->getRuntime(EscaperRuntime::class)->escape($return, $strategy, $charset, $autoescape);
     }

     // This is a normal render array, which is safe by definition, with
